Note: (unpack tuple func) — runtime first-class apply (TUP-11)
Note: Tests: zero-arg, single-arg, multi-arg, dynamic Function-value

use "@std"

Note: ===== Test 1: zero-arg =====
Note: 0-arg proc identifiers auto-call when referenced (EvaluateVariable line 150);
Note: pass the function as a value via a Function-typed lambda binding instead.
Function getFortyTwo = fn => 42
Tuple<<>> empty = <<>>
Int r1 = (unpack empty getFortyTwo)
(print (str r1))

Note: ===== Test 2: single-arg =====
proc doubler (Int: n)
    (mul n 2)
end proc
Tuple<<Int>> single = <<5>>
Int r2 = (unpack single doubler)
(print (str r2))

Note: ===== Test 3: multi-arg =====
proc addPair (Int: a, Int: b)
    (add a b)
end proc
Tuple<<Int, Int>> pair = <<3, 4>>
Int r3 = (unpack pair addPair)
(print (str r3))

Note: ===== Test 4: dynamic Function-value =====
Function f = fn Int a, Int b => (mul a b)
Tuple<<Int, Int>> mp = <<6, 7>>
Int r4 = (unpack mp f)
(print (str r4))

(print "test_unpack_runtime: PASSED")
